# Beginner Projects for AI Agent Course

This directory contains beginner-level projects designed to help participants apply the foundational concepts learned in the AI Agent Developer and Operator course. Each project focuses on practical implementation and reinforces key skills necessary for developing and operating AI agents.

## Project 1: Simple Chatbot

### Description
Develop a simple rule-based chatbot that can respond to basic user queries. This project will help you understand the fundamentals of natural language processing and user interaction.

### Objectives
- Implement basic text processing techniques.
- Create a set of predefined responses.
- Test the chatbot with various user inputs.

### Technologies Used
- Python
- NLTK (Natural Language Toolkit)

### Instructions
1. Set up your development environment.
2. Create a Python script for the chatbot.
3. Implement text processing functions.
4. Define a set of rules for responses.
5. Test the chatbot with sample queries.

---

## Project 2: Basic Recommendation System

### Description
Build a simple recommendation system that suggests items based on user preferences. This project will introduce you to collaborative filtering techniques.

### Objectives
- Understand user-item interaction.
- Implement a basic collaborative filtering algorithm.
- Evaluate the performance of the recommendation system.

### Technologies Used
- Python
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn

### Instructions
1. Gather a dataset of user preferences.
2. Preprocess the data using Pandas.
3. Implement a collaborative filtering algorithm.
4. Test the recommendation system with sample users.

---

## Project 3: Image Classification with Pre-trained Model

### Description
Utilize a pre-trained deep learning model to classify images. This project will demonstrate the power of transfer learning in AI development.

### Objectives
- Load a pre-trained model (e.g., MobileNet, ResNet).
- Fine-tune the model on a new dataset.
- Evaluate the model's performance on test images.

### Technologies Used
- Python
- TensorFlow/Keras
- Matplotlib for visualization

### Instructions
1. Download a dataset of images for classification.
2. Load the pre-trained model.
3. Fine-tune the model on your dataset.
4. Visualize the results using Matplotlib.

---

## Project 4: Basic Sentiment Analysis Tool

### Description
Create a simple sentiment analysis tool that can classify text as positive, negative, or neutral. This project will help you understand sentiment analysis techniques.

### Objectives
- Implement text preprocessing steps.
- Use a machine learning model for sentiment classification.
- Evaluate the model's accuracy on a test dataset.

### Technologies Used
- Python
- Scikit-learn
- NLTK or TextBlob

### Instructions
1. Gather a dataset of labeled text samples.
2. Preprocess the text data.
3. Train a sentiment analysis model using Scikit-learn.
4. Test the model and report the accuracy.

---

These beginner projects are designed to provide hands-on experience and reinforce the concepts learned in the course. Participants are encouraged to explore and expand upon these projects as they progress through the AI Agent Developer and Operator course.